;; it-prio-load.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-prio-load.s` (P2-SCALAR.4).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py it-prio-load.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "it-prio-load.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-prio-load.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05), against the reference behaviors MEASURED by probe `prio-load` (sail-riscv 0.14 AND" "spike 1.1.1-dev) before this guest existed — the leaf design records the measurements. The trap" "step is last. ⭐ x2 must NEVER be written: a trapping load retires no write, and the misalignment" "is judged BEFORE the boundary is crossed, so no data crossing exists (the mutation suite's census" "pins the empty arm).")
(expectations (program "it-prio-load.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 3) (never_written "x2") (step (n 0) (insn "lui x1, 0x40000") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000040000000"))) (derivation "0x40000 << 12 = 0x40000000; bit 31 is clear, so the sign extension adds nothing. Outside every region either platform declares — the unmapped half of the double fault.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-LUI-AUIPC)")) (step (n 1) (insn "addi x1, x1, 1") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000040000001"))) (derivation "0x40000000 + 1 = 0x40000001 — 1 mod 4, so a 4-byte load there is misaligned: the misaligned half of the double fault.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-ALU-IMM)")) (step (n 2) (insn "lw x2, x1, 0") (writes) (derivation "The effective address 0x40000001 is BOTH misaligned AND unmapped. D-MISALIGN-DATA judges the misalignment BEFORE the boundary is crossed, so load-address-misaligned wins: cause 0x04, tval = the address — measured identical on both references (probe prio-load) — and x2 is never written.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.6 (the EEI defines whether misaligned accesses are handled invisibly) — decision D-MISALIGN-DATA; RVI-RV64I §3.1.3")))
